# Checkpoint KV-cache dtype precedence and rollout

Memory type: playbook
Recorded: 2026-08-14T16:37:00.392730+00:00
Confidence: 0.98
Owner: Jamal Pierce
Tags: vllm, kv-cache, fp8, deployment, rollback, issue-34752

## Summary

Treat recognized checkpoint KV-cache quantization metadata as a storage-format contract: implicit or explicit auto adopts it; a matching explicit alias is canonicalized; a mismatched explicit override fails during configuration with guidance to use auto or the checkpoint dtype. Without metadata, preserve existing auto/model-dtype and supported explicit behavior. Preflight hardware/backend compatibility read-only, canary 3/10/30/70/100 with 30-minute holds, and rollback to a warm pinned revision while invalidating incompatible KV state.

## Outcome

Validated by syntax compilation and seven focused CPU configuration assertions; GPU backend checks remain required.

